{"items":[{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-63414"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-05T06:31:29.927137Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-05T06:31:29.927137Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-63414","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-10-30T22:49:47.431000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/Shopify/shopify_app/releases/tag/v23.0.3","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/63xxx/CVE-2026-63414.json","https://github.com/Shopify/shopify_app/security/advisories/GHSA-6j52-38f8-qhxr","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-63414","https://github.com/Shopify/shopify_app/commit/a09ccc04b9556cbb31c6d56ed81aeb6b9b6c0756","https://github.com/Shopify/shopify_app/pull/2081"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63414"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-63414","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-63414"},"summary":"Shopify App is a Rails engine for building Shopify applications. From 22.1.0 until 23.0.3, `token-exchange` authenticated controllers can expose a request-derived `shop` context instead of the identity from a verified Shopify ID token or active Shopify session. `current_shopify_domain` can resolve to the sanitized `shop` query parameter, so a request authenticated for one `shop` can cause application code to treat a different requested `shop` as current. Affected applications use `shopify_app` `token-exchange` authentication, accept authenticated requests with a `shop` query parameter, and rely on `current_shopify_domain` or `params[:shop]` for authorization, tenant lookup, stored access-token selection or `shop`-scoped data access. An attacker with a valid Shopify session token for one `shop` can supply another `shop` in that parameter and potentially obtain unauthorized application data or perform `shop`-scoped actions, depending on the application's authorization model. This issue is fixed in version 23.0.3.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Shopify App: Token exchange shop context confusion may allow cross-shop authorization bypass in affected apps","topics":["advisory","cwe-863"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-04T02:31:01.458228Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2024-27834"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-05T06:31:29.927137Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-05T06:31:29.927137Z","id":"osv:CVE-2024-27834","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2024-05-14T15:13:06.953000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://support.apple.com/kb/HT214100","https://support.apple.com/kb/HT214102","https://support.apple.com/kb/HT214104","https://support.apple.com/kb/HT214106","https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT214102","https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT214103","https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT214106","https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT214101","https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT214104","http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2024/05/21/1","http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2024/May/12","https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/ADCLQW54XN37VJZNYD3UKCYATJFIMYXG/","https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/WKIXADCW3O4R2OOSDZGPU55XQFE6NA3M/","http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2024/May/10","htt